{"title":"2022 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(🚀Fast_and_EZ!🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (🚀Fast and EZ!🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The midpoints of the four sides of a rectangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7cf360ae774e06e0a429d20e3cd6d1980d2db00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3,0), (2,0), (5,4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/98121c06337629a73bbef8fa46adf7d3220aca4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,4).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> What is the\narea of the rectangle? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbfd98561e1883ea5be03715c7dbe1acc3f4c6e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 25 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 40 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The midpoints of the four sides of every rectangle are the vertices of a rhombus whose area is half the area of the rectangle: Note that the diagonals of the rhombus have the same lengths as the sides of the rectangle.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/54903cd731afce17f477ba6ccb848724116e8aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(-3,0), B=(2,0), C=(5,4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2955e39df57390c606a887caefc4918915cfb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(0,4).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e84eb3b30456a70ab34b765c85e17bf227c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the vertices of a rhombus whose diagonals have lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa230178ad1cbf084bac4badfbd854e7a2d0fbc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced397074cb2000d04e1ba3d8aad803257c3041a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=2\\sqrt{5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" /> It follows that the dimensions of the rectangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1d8d49bd04ec238c372f249f77d023673c48431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b0502611c2bfd3edb13a644ac351679a230b4708.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"23\" /> so the area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e06fae7df7e244a4bd5493d1a7035063e641801b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{5}\\cdot2\\sqrt{5}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 40}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"175\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a rectangle has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d102b7c029f03c429abb7f49384232a3cd774d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> then the area of the quadrilateral formed by its midpoints is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78abfef0297151b100b580fc9e5799c02b8c7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{K}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"28\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Define points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e84eb3b30456a70ab34b765c85e17bf227c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as Solution 1 does. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e84eb3b30456a70ab34b765c85e17bf227c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of the rectangle, the rectangle's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2ceebf98aecc6c1a157ef5aeeeacf3ad98408d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2[ABCD].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> Now, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9daa1c163dd0918b45a34bf993c04936cd9b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac9acbd2aa203f8f640b80c9e075400433cae91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}\\parallel\\overline{CD}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> As the parallelogram's height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3867a04adfb63be21e0737a81a711e05a9f044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af40b246e6643721018b898f0960013a87b2dad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot5=20.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" /> Therefore, the area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bd9cbbae241a2f9ea940740bd73f3989035f6e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\cdot2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 40}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"136\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Fruitz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Graph paper is not permitted on the AMC 8. Still, blank scratch paper is provided, and with that, you can draw a makeshift coordinate plane and \"graph\" some dots. It doesn't have to be very exact, but do make reasonable estimates on the locations of the points. Once you graph the dots and look around, it becomes apparent that the only rectangle that would make sense would be if the length were from (-3,0) to (5,4), and the width would have to be from (0,4) to (2,0). With that in mind, use the distance formula to solve for the length and width. The distance formula is as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544f429c078dccf33580e9e33c26b4bb8a3c6f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"232\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSimply put the coordinates into the formula to get the distance between the two points. Using the formula, the length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac93bce8f2cc113170fcba1e35e7c59256dd6956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />, and the width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e6895445d6df3d71da8e88786be997603e1b9032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Now, multiply the length and width together to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b37512c816a6127b63d7498ad0ec227495be65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 40}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" /> ~Evžen D.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=vK4K2jqt5YqxWhhg&amp;t=3182\">https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=vK4K2jqt5YqxWhhg&amp;t=3182</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=2153\">https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=2153</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Fast_and_EZ.21.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(🚀Fast_and_EZ!🚀)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (🚀Fast and EZ!🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (🚀Fast and EZ!🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Bxp0coLo5r4?si=49fvyWZBrsutgpBt\">https://youtu.be/Bxp0coLo5r4?si=49fvyWZBrsutgpBt</a>\n</p><p>~ AMC8 Learning\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5Vti6QS7TfU\">https://youtu.be/5Vti6QS7TfU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1564\">https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1564</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.b